<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pyramid of the Magician</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pyramid of the Dwarf</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pyramid of the Magician is the tallest structure at the Maya city of Uxmal in Yucatán, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, about 35 metres high, with an unusual oval plan. It was built in several phases from about the 6th to the 10th century, each enclosing earlier temples. A Maya legend tells that a dwarf magician raised it in a single night, giving it its name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pyramid-of-the-magician.jpg" alt="Pyramid of the Magician" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rob Young from United Kingdom · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pyramid_of_the_Magician_(8264902976).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
